        "title": "feat: add sync-plan json output",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `crabbox sync-plan --json` for machine-readable sync preflight output.\n- Include candidate totals, dirty-delta totals, deleted tracked path count, guardrail status/reasons, and top file/dir rows.\n- Document the JSON contract and add a command-level regression test.\n\n## Why\n\n`sync-plan` already computes the same manifest that `run` uses, but the text-only output is awkward for CI checks and agent workflows that want to budget sync size before provisioning a remote box.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestSyncPlan|TestSyncManifest|TestHumanBytes|TestSortSyncPlanRows' -count=1`\n- `go test ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `node scripts/check-command-docs.mjs`\n- `node scripts/check-docs-links.mjs`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` attempted twice; both attempts were blocked by the Codex review engine reporting the workspace is out of credits.",
